---
title: Executive Memo - UK and European Family Leave Guidance
sourceType: internal_memo
date: 2026-02-10
jurisdiction: United Kingdom
language: en
register: corporate_standard
format: docx
---

Under UK statutory maternity and paternity guidelines, statutory paternity leave is restricted to two weeks following the birth of the child.

Employees taking statutory paternity leave must give formal notice to their HR business partner at least 15 weeks before the expected week of childbirth.

UK employees on maternity leave retain all contractual benefits except remuneration and are entitled to up to 52 weeks of maternity leave.
